(version 1)

# Custom design rules — comms transceiver board.
#
# Copied from hardware/conventions/jlcpcb_baseline.kicad_dru. Retune the
# width band below if the fabbed stackup changes.
#
# See kicad_jlcpcb_design_rules.md §5.3. KiCad has no live binding between
# the impedance profile and the stackup, so the width is computed once by
# hand and pinned here; this rule is what makes DRC flag a trace that
# drifts off it.
#
# Stackup: JLCPCB JLC04161H-7628, 4-layer 1.6 mm, L1 over a solid L2
# ground plane. L1<->L2 prepreg 0.2104 mm, er 4.4 (Nan Ya NP-155F 7628),
# giving 50 ohm microstrip at ~0.358 mm. Recompute with the JLCPCB
# impedance calculator if the stackup changes.

(rule "RF 50ohm microstrip width"
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'RF'")
  (constraint track_width (min 0.35mm) (opt 0.358mm) (max 0.37mm)))
